# `tributacion-conjunta-individual` research: `tributacion conjunta vs individual comparison surface`

Issue #547 (P1, NEEDS-DESIGN): an IRPF (Modelo 100) taxpayer with a spouse / unidad
familiar may file under tributacion individual or conjunta; the cheaper option turns on
the income split and the reduccion por tributacion conjunta (LIRPF art. 84.2). The tool
computes a single modelo run under whatever modality the profile declares and offers no
surface to compute both and report the favorable one. This research grounds the design in
the live M100 calculate path, the existing modality axis, and the household input model at
HEAD `298d6561` (branch `chore/eliminate-shims`).

## Findings

### F1 - The modality axis already exists and is live in the M100 cuota chain

The tributacion-conjunta-vs-individual axis is not new work. It is fully present at HEAD:

- Typed core enum: `RentaDeclaracionType` (`src/aeat/domain/contribuyente/_renta_codes.py:20`)
  - `INDIVIDUAL = "1"`, `JOINT = "2"`. Companion `SituacionFamiliar` StrEnum (art. 82
  family situation) governs conjunta eligibility.
- Profile fact + binding: the M100 registry binding `renta-2025-profile-declaration-type`
  (`bindings/0009-renta-2025-profile-declaration-type.toml`) reads profile key
  `filing_export.declaration_type` (XSD `TIPOTRIBUTACION`), `op = copy`, legal_ref
  `orden-hac-277-2026:art-3`. The `declaration_type` field is declared in
  `src/aeat/_data/registry/aeat/user_profile/schema.toml:838`.
- Live reduccion formula: `renta-2025-reduccion-art-84-conjunta`
  (`formulas/0179-renta-2025-reduccion-art-84-conjunta.toml`, and the 2024 sibling
  `0176-...`) targets casilla `0461` and computes, via `if_then_else` on the
  declaration-type and minor-children bindings: `3400` (matrimonio, modalidad 1a), `2150`
  (monoparental, modalidad 2a), `0` (individual). It is enrolled in the
  `renta-cuota-chain` construct `formulas` list
  (`constructs/0001-renta-cuota-chain.toml`), so the engine base-liquidable to cuota chain
  already consumes it.
- Provenance of the wiring: exec `2026-05-27-marcos-214-reduccion-art-84-S214` records
  casilla 0461 upgraded to `input_kind = computed` and the formula inserted before
  `renta-{2024,2025}-base-liquidable-general`, fixing the prior state where 0461 stayed 0
  even when the profile carried `declaration_type = 2`.

Consequence: running `calculate` with `declaration_type` set to "1" versus "2" already
yields a different base liquidable and a different cuota from the same engine. A comparison
surface needs no new calculation logic - only a way to drive the existing engine twice
under the two modality values and read each result.
